  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the toilet flush handle via pointing gesture and text",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the hand pointing at the flush handle, and the textual material 'the one piece of shit that just won't flush!' which humorously assigns blame to the flush handle. The pointing gesture and the text create a shared experience where the viewer identifies with the frustration, projecting themselves as the person experiencing the clogged toilet problem. The deictic nature of the pointing hand and the accusatory text create an implicit 'you' or 'me' projection onto the flush handle as the source of the annoyance.",
